{"name":"Sawdust","hex":"#f6e9cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sawdust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fine particles (dust) created by sawing wood or other material.","Food that is unpleasantly powdery and tasteless."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sprinkle with sawdust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sawdust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sawdust","blocks":[{"text":"Sawdust is a by-product or waste product of woodworking operations such as sawing, sanding, milling and routing. It is composed of very small chips of wood. These operations can be performed by woodworking machinery, portable power tools or by use of hand tools. In some manufacturing industries it can be a significant fire hazard and source of occupational dust exposure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Saw_dust_%28Zaagsel%29.jpg/330px-Saw_dust_%28Zaagsel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sawdust","wikidata":"Q816713"},{"title":"Sawdust (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sawdust is a compilation album by American rock band the Killers, released on November 9, 2007, by Island Records. The album consists mostly of B-sides, but also includes a number of previously unreleased tracks. The songs on the album were recorded between 2002 and 2007."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/30/The_Killers_-_Sawdust.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sawdust_(album)","wikidata":"Q265550"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg/500px-Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Ogatan%28JapaneseBriquetteCharcoal%29.jpg/1280px-Ogatan%28JapaneseB